        <briefdescription>
<para>Computes and propagates gradients for the addition operation. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Implements the backward pass for elementwise addition by passing the incoming gradient unchanged to both parent tensors. Since the derivative of addition with respect to each input is unity, the gradient is propagated without modification. The method calls <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradAdd_1a76c8bf1698dddd5eb815bb77a612f674" kindref="member">backward()</ref> on each parent&apos;s <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> to continue the backpropagation process.</para>
<para>When higherDerivative is false, gradient tracking is disabled on the saved tensors to prevent construction of a new computational graph during backpropagation.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>inputGradient</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The gradient of the loss with respect to the output of the addition operation </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>higherDerivative</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If true, enables construction of a computational graph during the backward pass for higher-order derivatives; if false, disables gradient tracking on saved tensors </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
