    <briefdescription>
<para>Gradient function for elementwise tensor addition. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradAdd" kindref="compound">GradAdd</ref> class represents the addition operation in the computational graph, computing gradients for the elementwise sum of two tensors. For the operation <formula id="6">$C = A + B$</formula>, the gradient computation follows from the identity:    <formula id="7">\[    \frac{\partial C}{\partial A} = 1, \quad \frac{\partial C}{\partial B}
= 1
\]</formula></para>
<para>During backpropagation, the incoming gradient  <formula id="8">$\frac{\partial L}{\partial
C}$</formula> is passed unchanged to both parent tensors according to the chain rule:    <formula id="9">\[    \frac{\partial L}{\partial A} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C} \cdot
\frac{\partial C}{\partial A} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C}
\]</formula>    <formula id="10">\[    \frac{\partial L}{\partial B} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C} \cdot
\frac{\partial C}{\partial B} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C}
\]</formula></para>
<para>This <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> saves copies of both input tensors, though they are not strictly required for the gradient computation of addition. The saved tensors may be used for higher-order derivative computations or for consistency with the gradient function interface.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> for the base class from which this class derives. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradAddScalar" kindref="compound">GradAddScalar</ref> for the gradient function for tensor-scalar addition. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
